            <h2 data-start="158" data-end="197"><font size="+3"
                face="Calibri" color="#ff0000">Current News</font></h2>
            <p><font size="+3" color="#cc0000"><b>Registration for the
                  2026 State/Sectional Target is posted.</b></font></p>
            <p><font size="+3" color="#cc0000"><b><font face="Calibri">FITA




                    Field</font> results and records have been updated
                  and posted.<br>
                </b></font><br>
            </p>
            <h2 data-start="158" data-end="197">Meeting minutes - <a
                href="Board26fld.pdf">Feb 6, 2026</a>, <a
                href="Board26fld.pdf">2026 Field<br>
              </a></h2>
            <p><font size="+1">NFAA is going to have a new format for
                the Sectional Outdoor.&nbsp; It is a 12 target round
                half round with 3 arrows per target.&nbsp; It is no
                walk-ups and no fans.&nbsp; For the Field they are
                dropping the 80W and the 45W.&nbsp; The 15 yarder will
                be shot on the bunny face (20cm).&nbsp; You can also
                think of it as an International with the Bunny and 15
                yarder added to it.&nbsp; We are offering both the 14,
                14, 14 and the new 12, 12, 12 at the State Field as
                separate shoots which can be shot either day (or you can
                shoot the same one twice).&nbsp; Both count towards
                shooter of the year.&nbsp; Targets 1-14 are the 14
                rounds and targets 15-28 will be the 12.target rounds..<br>
              </font> </p>
            <font size="+1"> </font>
            <p><font size="+1">NFAA is going to offer a Sectional
                Target.&nbsp; Sections have a choice of a Classic 600 or
                a 900.&nbsp; The SE Section is going with the 900.&nbsp;
                We are going to split the 900 between Gold Coast and
                Gator.</font><br>
            </p>
